WEBVTT

01:31.000 --> 01:36.000
Any Man Who Wears Glasses
Cannot Be a Bad Man

01:38.250 --> 01:41.500
Hard-working, hard-working Hayato-kun.

01:41.500 --> 01:45.250
All alone, all alone,
cleaning up the room!

01:49.000 --> 01:51.360
It's so much cleaner now!

01:58.270 --> 02:01.100
So that's where you've been!

02:01.100 --> 02:05.300
And here I thought you got blown to bits.

02:06.480 --> 02:08.260
You sure did work hard!

02:14.100 --> 02:16.020
Ah...

02:18.530 --> 02:21.280
Dustpan, dustpan...

02:21.280 --> 02:23.580
I think it's around here.

02:35.040 --> 02:37.300
Glasses and Us

02:35.040 --> 02:37.300
The Glasses Club albums!

02:37.300 --> 02:39.720
So this is where they were!

02:43.790 --> 02:47.940
Law of Cleaning: You will always find an
old album and get sucked into its nostalgia.

02:47.930 --> 02:51.000
Th-These are... These are...

02:51.160 --> 02:53.480
...my senpai back in their first year!

02:53.480 --> 02:57.520
Wow, even back then, they were taking
proper commemorative photos!

02:58.840 --> 03:00.500
Giant Glasses!

03:03.640 --> 03:04.890
X-Ray Glasses Mk. 13

03:07.600 --> 03:08.730
Glasses on Glasses

03:11.520 --> 03:12.810
X-Ray Glasses Mk. 15

03:15.690 --> 03:16.730
Yukiya's hair is too long! (lol)

03:19.240 --> 03:20.320
Afro Glasses

03:24.700 --> 03:26.930
What are they doing?

03:26.930 --> 03:32.020
But why are the pictures of all three
of them together so out of focus?

03:34.590 --> 03:36.890
This is when we first years
joined the club!

03:39.400 --> 03:41.280
That's right!

03:41.280 --> 03:44.340
I forgot Mitsuki had glasses
like that back then.

03:44.340 --> 03:49.280
<i>Shortly after this, I would
uncover a shocking truth.</i>

03:49.280 --> 03:53.920
<i>But I didn't realize it at all at the time.</i>

03:57.400 --> 03:58.450
Huh?

04:09.200 --> 04:14.930
I'm not in them?

04:16.300 --> 04:17.750
Is that what this is?!

04:17.750 --> 04:21.650
I was certain of my existence,
but I actually died a long time ago,

04:18.480 --> 04:18.970
Existence

04:21.650 --> 04:23.920
and even though I am who I am,
I'm not me at all!

04:23.410 --> 04:23.920
Existence

04:23.920 --> 04:25.300
In other words, a ghost—

04:27.660 --> 04:28.650
Clunk?

04:29.730 --> 04:32.700
Yep! I'm alive!

04:32.900 --> 04:34.750
That means it's just a fluke, right?

04:34.750 --> 04:38.600
It's just a fluke that there are
no pictures with me in them.

04:41.430 --> 04:43.520
<i>Yes, that's right.</i>

04:43.520 --> 04:46.230
<i>The blue sky stretching on endlessly...</i>

04:47.260 --> 04:51.960
<i>As I looked at it, I thought back
to that day I can never forget.</i>

04:52.460 --> 04:56.230
<i>The events of the entrance
ceremony that changed my life</i>

04:56.230 --> 04:58.490
<i>were reborn brilliantly in my memory.</i>

04:56.230 --> 05:01.240
1 Year Ago
Himaraya 3rd Technical High School

04:59.760 --> 05:01.240
Man...

05:01.240 --> 05:04.260
The cherry blossoms are
slow to bloom this year.

05:01.240 --> 05:07.260
*Dramatization

05:04.260 --> 05:06.780
And today is my entrance ceremony...

05:06.780 --> 05:09.080
It feels lonely without them.

05:14.010 --> 05:17.620
Moving on, I will now
introduce the Glasses Club.

05:18.060 --> 05:20.140
Would the Glasses Club members come forward?

05:20.420 --> 05:23.930
Glasses Club? What's that?

05:21.230 --> 05:23.300
Would the Glasses Club members come forward?

05:24.260 --> 05:27.170
Well, as the members of the Glasses Club
don't appear to be here,

05:27.170 --> 05:28.160
we'll move on to—

05:27.520 --> 05:29.640
Hold it!

05:35.730 --> 05:36.780
What's that?!

05:36.780 --> 05:38.150
Oh, hell...

05:59.370 --> 06:01.500
No glasses!

06:01.700 --> 06:04.260
No

06:04.260 --> 06:05.310
life!

06:19.420 --> 06:20.990
Do his glasses not have lenses in them?

06:21.250 --> 06:23.130
Idiot! Get out of the way!

06:37.810 --> 06:39.360
Cherry blossoms?

06:45.090 --> 06:47.850
And that's when I thought,

06:48.310 --> 06:52.290
"Wow, he sure is a manly guy."

06:48.310 --> 07:45.450
Glasses
Club!

06:48.310 --> 07:45.450
Moving true stories of
modern-day Glasses Men

06:52.290 --> 06:56.100
When my dad was alive, he used to say...

06:56.100 --> 07:00.240
"Any man who wears glasses
cannot be a bad man."

07:00.460 --> 07:05.170
Q: What about that time he made you buy curry bread
and beat you up for bringing back the wrong change?

07:02.720 --> 07:05.350
What? These glasses, you ask?

07:05.350 --> 07:09.200
Yes, that's right, great observation.

07:09.200 --> 07:11.160
They're a memento from my dad.

07:11.160 --> 07:14.730
I loved my dad for his strength and kindness.

07:14.730 --> 07:16.180
Thinking back on it now,

07:16.180 --> 07:19.480
these glasses might have been
what introduced me...

07:19.480 --> 07:21.620
to the Glasses Club.

07:22.100 --> 07:26.570
Q: Why is it that, at that time, you bought coffee
milk instead of the fruit milk he asked you for?

07:23.330 --> 07:25.960
The reason I'm here, you ask?

07:27.390 --> 07:33.870
I sensed that as long as I was with him,
my youth would consist of 100% manliness.

07:33.870 --> 07:36.600
And that's the reason why!

07:38.570 --> 07:40.560
Okay, cut!

07:40.560 --> 07:42.530
Great work, everyone!

07:42.530 --> 07:45.450
Great work! Great work!

07:45.450 --> 07:48.570
Great work! Great work!

07:48.570 --> 07:51.700
Yamada-chan, your lighting
was perfect as always!

07:51.700 --> 08:08.950
Soma Akira      Minabe Yukiya      Hachimine Takuma      Kamatani Mitsuki

07:54.400 --> 07:56.420
Well, I did it.

07:56.410 --> 07:59.040
I filmed the very dawn of my life!

08:14.880 --> 08:17.210
Finally finished!

08:17.900 --> 08:21.300
I guess it's not totally
back to the way it was...

08:21.300 --> 08:24.370
But it's much cleaner now!

08:24.810 --> 08:28.920
Maybe they'll be so moved by
my love for the Glasses Club

08:28.920 --> 08:32.120
that they'll ask me to become
the vice president!

08:32.210 --> 08:32.980
-dent!

08:33.100 --> 08:33.880
-dent!

08:33.980 --> 08:34.630
-dent!

08:34.720 --> 08:35.540
-dent!

08:51.310 --> 08:52.280
Huh?

08:58.510 --> 09:01.540
Just as I thought. Our new club room is...

09:01.310 --> 09:02.890
Glasses Club

09:05.460 --> 09:06.620
Really good!

09:07.150 --> 09:09.270
Old Club Room

09:09.570 --> 09:11.730
Current Club Room

09:09.860 --> 09:12.160
It sure is, Soma-senpai!

09:13.820 --> 09:15.370
This wallpaper...

09:15.370 --> 09:19.130
I picked it out. Isn't it nice?

09:22.410 --> 09:23.480
Look!

09:23.480 --> 09:26.260
My hands are moving like a god's!

09:26.260 --> 09:27.880
Wow! That's amazing!

09:28.170 --> 09:31.300
What's going on here?!

09:37.730 --> 09:41.180
Why did you all leave me out of this?

09:41.550 --> 09:43.080
What's wrong, Hayato?

09:43.080 --> 09:45.260
What are you so worked up about?

09:45.260 --> 09:47.290
Ho... Ho... Ho...

09:47.270 --> 09:48.810
You've gone hog wild?

09:47.290 --> 09:48.810
Glasses Hog

09:48.810 --> 09:51.150
Ho-How could you do this
to me?! The club room!

09:52.250 --> 09:56.970
Why didn't you tell me about
the new club room?!

09:56.970 --> 10:00.820
I only heard about it now when
I asked Mr. Shirogane about it!

10:00.820 --> 10:02.440
Oh, really?

10:02.440 --> 10:05.580
I asked Takuma to spread the word
to everyone yesterday, but...

10:05.710 --> 10:09.580
Starting tomorrow,
the club room will be the one
two floors up. See you there!
-Takuma

10:06.500 --> 10:09.580
I handed out enough for everyone.

10:09.820 --> 10:13.300
I gave yours to Mit-chan to give to you.

10:15.040 --> 10:17.080
Mitsuki! You did thi—

10:17.330 --> 10:18.400
Oink?

10:18.400 --> 10:20.470
You're not fooling anyone!

10:20.470 --> 10:22.320
You're the one who's not fooling anyone!

10:22.320 --> 10:23.480
Cut it out!

10:24.630 --> 10:27.100
My eyes! My eyes!

10:27.100 --> 10:30.690
I just forgot to give it to you
because of those fake glasses of yours.

10:30.690 --> 10:33.110
My fake glasses have
nothing to do with it!

10:33.110 --> 10:35.150
It has everything to do with it.

10:35.150 --> 10:37.390
For someone with fake glasses
to join the Glasses Club,

10:37.390 --> 10:42.070
even just as a provisional
member, is a big problem!

10:43.670 --> 10:47.230
You said that before, too.
Am I still a provisional member?

10:47.230 --> 10:48.540
You are.

10:49.060 --> 10:50.570
Is that true?

10:53.050 --> 10:56.360
I was hoping you'd explain it
clearly someday, Soma-senpai.

10:56.360 --> 10:59.840
Why did you let a guy who doesn't
wear glasses into the Glasses Club?

11:02.100 --> 11:04.850
Why, you ask? Hey, Yukiya?

11:05.080 --> 11:06.090
Yeah.

11:07.590 --> 11:08.610
Here.

11:10.870 --> 11:12.350
What's this?

11:12.690 --> 11:14.450
It's the Kimata family tree.

11:15.360 --> 11:18.780
My family tree is publicly available?

11:18.780 --> 11:20.610
Well, with your family being what it is...

11:20.860 --> 11:22.070
Family?

11:22.740 --> 11:27.290
Oh, Hayato-kun's ancestor
was Ouchi Yoshitaka.

11:27.290 --> 11:29.120
Huh?!

11:31.370 --> 11:34.210
So, who's Ouchi Yoshitaka?

11:31.770 --> 11:36.630
Ouchi Yoshitaka

11:34.210 --> 11:36.630
Good question!

11:38.080 --> 11:40.570
The medieval lord who received

11:40.570 --> 11:43.260
the first pair of glasses in Japan
from Francisco Xavier.

11:43.260 --> 11:45.520
His name was Ouchi Yoshitaka.

11:44.120 --> 11:46.140
Ouchi Yoshitaka

11:47.340 --> 11:49.630
That's got a great ring to it!

11:49.630 --> 11:50.890
I get it.

11:51.260 --> 11:53.330
So if that family tree is right,

11:53.330 --> 11:57.650
Hayato-kun's family has an incredible
connection to glasses. So that's why.

11:57.650 --> 11:58.650
That <i>is</i> why!

11:59.140 --> 12:02.180
I took the Glasses Soul that permeates
Hayato's blood into account

12:02.180 --> 12:03.930
and permitted him
provisional membership!

12:03.910 --> 12:08.160
Glasses Soul

12:04.490 --> 12:08.160
Piggybacking on your ancestors isn't fair!

12:08.160 --> 12:11.580
This guy.

12:08.330 --> 12:11.380
They have nothing to do
with this guy here right now!

12:11.380 --> 12:12.670
It's fine!

12:12.880 --> 12:18.310
Basically, it means I have a more official
connection to glasses than anyone.

12:20.180 --> 12:25.560
Wow, I see! So that's how it is!

12:25.560 --> 12:29.430
My family wore the first glasses in Japan!

12:26.720 --> 12:30.680
Celebrating the first glasses in Japan

12:30.990 --> 12:32.390
Yahoo!

12:33.240 --> 12:36.350
He looks like he's feeling better now.

12:33.390 --> 12:35.300
Glasses! Glasses!

12:35.300 --> 12:38.400
My ancestor wore them first in Japan!

12:37.440 --> 12:39.620
Glasses truly are incredible!

12:38.400 --> 12:40.440
Glasses! Glasses!

12:39.620 --> 12:41.950
Our circle of friendship is united by glasses!

12:41.950 --> 12:42.700
Okay!

12:43.230 --> 12:45.410
To commemorate our first
activity in the new club room,

12:45.410 --> 12:46.830
let's take a group picture!

12:46.830 --> 12:47.870
Sounds good!

12:48.440 --> 12:49.540
Hayato! The camera!

12:49.700 --> 12:50.700
Right!

12:51.080 --> 12:55.170
Yeah, because there are definitely
no lenses in his glasses.

12:55.540 --> 12:57.370
Here we go!

12:57.380 --> 12:58.670
Glasses...

12:58.670 --> 12:59.710
...Club!

13:04.380 --> 13:10.930
Provisional
Member
Kimata
Hayato

13:04.380 --> 13:10.930
Kamatani
Mitsuki

13:04.380 --> 13:10.930
Minabe                  Soma
Yukiya                   Akira

13:04.380 --> 13:10.930
Hachimine
Takuma

13:30.700 --> 13:33.500
He's not in here.

13:34.660 --> 13:39.670
The Current Strongest Frames

13:43.090 --> 13:44.800
Hey, Minabe.

13:46.960 --> 13:52.060
Hey! You can't call someone
and then fall asleep on them.

13:54.900 --> 13:56.250
You're awake?

14:20.380 --> 14:22.140
Don't do things to confuse people!

14:25.630 --> 14:29.260
Yukiya Special:                                                     With these, you're
Wakey-Eye Stickers                                                 all set for class!

14:37.460 --> 14:39.390
Hey, Minabe!

14:58.620 --> 14:59.460
1 hour has passed.

15:05.390 --> 15:06.420
What is it?

15:06.420 --> 15:08.550
Don't give me that!

15:08.720 --> 15:11.880
You're the one who wanted to
use the work room after school

15:11.880 --> 15:13.680
and asked me to meet you there!

15:13.680 --> 15:15.720
Oh, that's right.

15:15.940 --> 15:19.380
I'm sorry. I hadn't completed
my daily routine yet today.

15:19.380 --> 15:20.900
Daily routine?

15:20.900 --> 15:23.240
I need an exactly 1-hour afternoon nap.

15:25.730 --> 15:27.250
So that's what that was.

15:28.460 --> 15:29.370
Glasses.

15:38.370 --> 15:40.570
You don't have Glasses Club today?

15:41.470 --> 15:43.880
Akira caught a cold.

15:45.680 --> 15:47.760
That's right, he wasn't in class.

15:58.990 --> 16:02.250
So? What are you doing?

16:03.150 --> 16:05.440
I'm researching frame strength.

16:09.250 --> 16:14.450
The development of X-Ray Glasses
requires this kind of effort every day.

16:16.090 --> 16:17.250
I see.

16:20.430 --> 16:21.920
But...

16:27.920 --> 16:29.170
It's so tedious.

16:33.150 --> 16:34.140
Yes.

17:00.700 --> 17:02.450
Bad Luck

18:27.920 --> 18:32.710
<i>When Minabe's around,
all we have is bad luck.</i>

18:37.220 --> 18:39.390
<i>Minabe's a bad luck charm!</i>

18:45.390 --> 18:48.390
<i>Hey! Keep away from me,
bad luck charm!</i>

19:06.550 --> 19:08.300
What happened to you?

19:12.590 --> 19:15.050
I see you're still a real clumsy kid.

20:03.260 --> 20:04.890
<i>What happened to you?</i>

20:04.890 --> 20:06.220
<i>You fell down?</i>

20:06.220 --> 20:08.810
<i>You must be a real clumsy kid.</i>

20:10.560 --> 20:12.520
<i>Here, wipe off your glasses.</i>

20:19.120 --> 20:20.120
Here.

20:27.790 --> 20:28.930
How's your cold?

20:29.660 --> 20:31.120
I just cured it with sheer willpower!

20:31.120 --> 20:32.120
I see.

20:34.940 --> 20:36.340
Is that...

20:39.380 --> 20:41.100
The current strongest frames!

20:41.650 --> 20:43.100
You finished the new ones?

20:44.200 --> 20:46.130
Yukiya, you're a genius!

20:46.130 --> 20:49.000
I'm psyched now! All right!

20:51.920 --> 20:53.480
The former strongest frames!

21:01.380 --> 21:02.380
Now for...

21:05.750 --> 21:07.240
The showdown!

21:15.920 --> 21:17.330
This is tedious.

21:18.270 --> 21:19.220
Yeah...

21:20.290 --> 21:21.940
However...

21:22.900 --> 21:25.980
The strongest frames belong to me!

21:26.600 --> 21:28.480
You know they belong to me!

23:11.950 --> 23:14.410
In this world, there are many
animals that wear glasses!

23:12.950 --> 23:24.340
Glasses

23:14.240 --> 23:14.700
They exist!

23:14.410 --> 23:16.460
Spectacled monkey! Spectacled
porpoise! Spectacled flying fox!

23:14.700 --> 23:15.330
Spectacled Monkey

23:15.330 --> 23:24.340
Spectacled Monkey      Spectacled Porpoise

23:15.790 --> 23:24.340
Spectacled Flying Fox

23:16.450 --> 23:18.710
However, they do not
actually wear glasses!

23:18.710 --> 23:20.460
Yeah, they just have big eyes, right?

23:20.460 --> 23:23.130
That's why we're going to
put glasses on all of them!

23:22.480 --> 23:24.330
Put glasses on all of them!

23:23.140 --> 23:24.330
Roger!

23:24.340 --> 23:25.960
No glasses, no life!

23:30.600 --> 23:32.010
Metal half rim.

23:32.340 --> 23:33.820
Tomorrow's horoscope:

23:34.390 --> 23:38.100
Be careful not to let your
wiPad run out of power.
